Marquis Software Solutions — IG-2026-010

Status: 🔴 Confirmed breach / root-cause litigation active
Priority: CRITICAL
Sector: Financial Technology
Incident Type: Ransomware + data exfiltration
Threat Actor: Unknown
Affected Population: Approximately 780K reported by PKWARE
Security Vendor Involved: SonicWall
Root Cause: Disputed
Last Reviewed: 2026-08-19

Confirmed
Marquis Software Solutions suffered unauthorized network access on August 14, 2025.
Marquis characterizes the event as ransomware.
Certain client data was accessed.
The affected information included PII belonging to customers of financial institutions served by Marquis.
SonicWall separately experienced unauthorized access involving its MySonicWall cloud-backup service.
SonicWall ultimately confirmed that firewall configuration backup files associated with all customers who had used that service were accessed.
SonicWall says those files contained encrypted credentials and configuration information.
SonicWall warned possession of those files could increase the risk of targeted attacks.
Marquis used SonicWall firewalls and had used the SonicWall cloud-backup feature.
Marquis filed suit against SonicWall in February 2026.
Consumer litigation related to the Marquis breach has been consolidated in federal court.
Alleged by Marquis
SonicWall's cloud incident began months before SonicWall publicly disclosed it.
A February 2025 API code change created an exploitable weakness.
Attackers could obtain firewall configuration backups without proper authentication.
Stolen configuration information included credentials and MFA recovery/scratch codes.
The attacker used SonicWall-derived information to bypass Marquis's firewall.
SonicWall initially told Marquis it was not affected.
SonicWall failed to provide Marquis timely information after Marquis requested assistance.
The SonicWall incident directly caused or materially enabled the Marquis ransomware compromise.
Not established as fact
The identity of the Marquis attacker.
The identity of the SonicWall attacker as the same actor.
A forensic chain proving one actor possessed both datasets.
A publicly confirmed CVE linking the two incidents.
The exact credential or secret used against Marquis.
Whether the firewall was bypassed exclusively through data obtained from SonicWall.
Whether another initial-access path existed.
The exact attacker dwell time.
Whether all approximately 780,000 individuals belong to one consolidated notification universe.
Whether courts will ultimately accept Marquis's causation theory.
